{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And you shall remember HaShem your Elohim, for it is He who gives you strength to make wealth</b>. It is well known that Israel are mighty men and men of valor in battle, for they are compared to lions — \"and a wolf shall tear\" — and the kings of Canaan defeated them in battle. Therefore He said: if you think \"my strength and the might of my hand has made me this wealth,\" you shall remember HaShem, who brought you out from Egypt, where you had no strength and might of hand at all; and you shall remember further that in the wilderness, where you had no means to survive, He made all your needs for you. If so, then even this wealth that you made with your strength — HaShem is the one who gave you the strength to make it. And if you forget HaShem, your strength and your remnant will fail and you will perish as they perished, for all who forsake HaShem shall fail.\n\nAnd He returned to bring yet another proof that you should not think \"my strength and the might of my hand,\" etc., and He said (Deuteronomy 9:1): \"Hear, O Israel\" — a true word from my mouth — \"for these nations are greater and mightier than you.\" How will you defeat them in battle? Moreover, they have great and fortified cities reaching to the heavens — how will you conquer them? Furthermore, there is a great and tall people there, the sons of the Anakim, which you know from the spies who saw them, and you have heard from days of old that no man can stand before them. And when all this becomes clear to you, you must know and believe from this day forward that you will not be able to overcome them at all, until you know in your heart that HaShem, who passes before you, is a devouring fire, and it is He who will destroy them and subdue them — not the strength and might of hand that was given to you, but the hand of HaShem did this against the mightiest among them.\n\nAnd this is an allusion to what is said (Joshua 10:11): \"And HaShem cast down upon them great stones from the heavens,\" and similarly it says there (the passage reads): \"and there was no day like it before it or after it... for HaShem fought for Israel.\" And the fortified cities that He mentioned here allude to the wall of Jericho, which fell before the Ark. And this is what David said (Psalms 44:4): \"For not by their sword did they possess the land, and their arm did not save them, but Your right hand and Your arm and the light of Your countenance, for You desired them\" — \"Your right hand and Your arm\" against the mighty ones, \"and the light of Your countenance, for You desired them\" among those slain in battle, for He gave them strength over them. And this is what Scripture further says (Amos 2:9): \"And I destroyed the Amorite from before them, whose height was like the height of cedars and who was strong as the oaks, and I destroyed his fruit from above and his roots from beneath.\" He singled out the Amorite because he was the mightiest among them, and HaShem is the one who destroys him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The citation marked (דברים ח':י\"ד) appears misplaced in context; Ramban seems to be quoting Joshua 10:12–14 rather than Deuteronomy 8:14, and I have translated the reference phrase hyper-literally without correcting it. The phrase שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל דְּבַר אֱמֶת מִפִּי (\"Hear, O Israel — a true word from my mouth\") is hyper-literal; the syntax is unusual and may reflect a textual difficulty."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:13.720740717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}